WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.101
♪ (SENTIMENTAL PIANO MUSIC
PLAYS) ♪

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:04.870
<i> Hi. It's me, Adrienne.</i>

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.406
Somebody's agreed
to let me make a movie again.

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:11.678
That never fails to surprise me
and delight me.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:17.617
She craved having
her voice heard,
and her vision being out there.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.352
ELAINE LANGBAUM:<i> From
when she was five years old,</i>

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:22.688
<i>when she was in kindergarten,
 she always stood out.</i>

00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:23.990
It was always Adrienne.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:29.195
It happened quickly.
In no time, she was the star
of this indie, cult film.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:32.031
"I'm sitting in a diner,
freaked beyond belief.

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:33.333
<i>What have we learned here?</i>

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.568 line:0%
<i> Write it
 and direct it yourself."</i>

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.236 line:0%
She really knew what she wanted.

00:00:37.336 --> 00:00:38.904
<i>She had such a clear idea of it.</i>

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:40.139
You come in, you rush in.

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:41.474
Okay. I messed it up
a little bit.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:42.908
ADRIENNE SHELLY:
It's fine. I don't care.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:46.178
SPEAKER:
<i>Her greatest joy was that child.</i>

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.348
ANDY OSTROY:<i> She was
the happiest I'd ever seen her.</i>

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:51.217
<i> I went to bed that night
 the luckiest guy alive.</i>

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:55.555
<i>By the next night, I was living
the worst nightmare imaginable.</i>

00:00:57.189 --> 00:00:59.158 line:0%
BRIAN:
My phone rings, and you said,

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.227
"Brian, get up here.
Adrienne's dead."

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:06.199
I just remember I fell to the
ground and I started screaming.

00:01:06.265 --> 00:01:07.166
♪ (INTENSE MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:01:07.566 --> 00:01:10.603
ANDY:<i> I get a call
from the detective, and he said,</i>

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.239
"Andrew, we arrested the guy
who killed Adrienne."

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:15.842
<i>Not a minute of every day
 goes by</i>

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.277
<i>without me thinking of Adrienne,</i>

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.879
<i> and what my daughter,
 Sophie, has lost.</i>

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:21.748
<i> What the world has lost.</i>

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:27.887
This was gonna be her moment.
How are we here and she's not?

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:32.424
I just have a very specific
kind of satisfaction

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:35.661
<i> when I see</i> Waitress
<i> on the Broadway marquee.</i>

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:39.966
ADRIENNE:<i> I was going for a tone
where you can find what's funny</i>

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.333
in what's painful,

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.504
<i>which has always kind of been
my strategy, anyway, in life.</i>

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.641
ANDY: You're almost the same age
as her, here.

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:51.577
"Don't be afraid of dying.
Be afraid of never living."

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.681
♪ (SENTIMENTAL PIANO MUSIC
PLAYS) ♪

